WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:03.050
VICTOR DAVIS HANSON: What is
the United Nations going to do?

00:00:03.050 --> 00:00:04.758
And the answer is they
can't do anything.

00:00:08.490 --> 00:00:11.940
In the ancient world,
Socrates, of all people,

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:15.300
said that he was not a
citizen of Athens alone,

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:17.010
he was a citizen of the world.

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:19.980
Our term cosmopolitan
comes from that concept,

00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:23.640
that he had affinities
with all the city-states

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:26.340
and, indeed, with all
the people in the world.

00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:29.520
In a very cynical fashion,
when Alexander the Great

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:34.350
in the latter fourth century BC
at the demise of the city-state

00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:39.570
went into Asia Minor and then on
to conquer the Persian empire,

00:00:39.570 --> 00:00:42.180
he needed a propaganda
talking point.

00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:44.520
And one of it was he
was going to usher

00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:48.420
in what he called the
Brotherhood of Man,

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:51.480
a new ecumenical idea that
whether you were Persian

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:53.440
or Greek, you were a human.

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:54.480
It sounds wonderful.

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:58.200
But the idea was that
enlightened rulers

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:00.420
from the Hellenic
world would spread

00:01:00.420 --> 00:01:03.930
their superior civilization
all over the world.

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:05.519
And it didn't last very well.

00:01:05.519 --> 00:01:08.640
In Roman times, Romans
being far more practical,

00:01:08.640 --> 00:01:10.650
they didn't talk
about globalization

00:01:10.650 --> 00:01:12.630
as much as reified it.

00:01:12.630 --> 00:01:13.890
They made it concrete.

00:01:13.890 --> 00:01:17.250
But immediately, there
were voices within Rome

00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:21.120
that said the further a
sovereign nation expands

00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:23.880
and globalizes,
the more difficult

00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:28.770
it is to maintain the solidarity
of the people, the purity

00:01:28.770 --> 00:01:30.870
of the original
founding concepts.

00:01:30.870 --> 00:01:33.870
The more we think we're
making people into Romans,

00:01:33.870 --> 00:01:35.940
the more they think
they are making us

00:01:35.940 --> 00:01:38.400
into other peoples
other than Romans.

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:41.490
One of the problems that the
globalists or cosmopolitans

00:01:41.490 --> 00:01:43.650
learned very early
in the 20th century

00:01:43.650 --> 00:01:46.200
during the progressive
movement was

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:50.820
when you surrender sovereignty
to these international bodies,

00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:53.280
then who is the police?

00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:55.150
Who polices the police?

00:01:55.150 --> 00:01:57.510
So the League of Nations,
which was envisioned

00:01:57.510 --> 00:02:00.600
under Woodrow Wilson's
Versailles agenda,

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:06.000
for a very brief time seemed to
be successful in adjudicating

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:09.570
international disputes of trade
or jurisdiction or borders

00:02:09.570 --> 00:02:14.940
until Adolf Hitler or the
Japanese militarists or Josef

00:02:14.940 --> 00:02:17.820
Stalin said, I don't
need to listen to you.

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:22.440
And so World War II doomed
the first incarnation

00:02:22.440 --> 00:02:25.110
of a united group of nations,
the League of Nations.

00:02:25.110 --> 00:02:28.260
After World War II, the
same suspicious idea

00:02:28.260 --> 00:02:30.960
resurfaced with
the United Nations.

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:34.320
But this time, we were going
to have a Security Council.

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:36.930
And they were going to be
the world's top powers,

00:02:36.930 --> 00:02:39.300
the strongest, the
most successful,

00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:41.400
and then they could
be the enforcer.

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:44.850
But the problem, of course, was
that very early on the Soviet

00:02:44.850 --> 00:02:47.940
Union was not the
solution to the problem,

00:02:47.940 --> 00:02:50.250
but it was the problem itself.

00:02:50.250 --> 00:02:52.920
Because there's always going
to be some country who's

00:02:52.920 --> 00:02:56.670
powerful by breaking
the rules and going

00:02:56.670 --> 00:02:58.950
beyond its own prerogative.

00:02:58.950 --> 00:03:01.650
In other words, an
anti-democratic China

00:03:01.650 --> 00:03:04.890
that has currently a million
and a half people in camps,

00:03:04.890 --> 00:03:07.260
and yet, they're on
the United Nations,

00:03:07.260 --> 00:03:09.700
and they're a
citizen of the world.

00:03:09.700 --> 00:03:13.110
And if the United
Nations would decide

00:03:13.110 --> 00:03:16.710
that the Chinese, contrary
to the UN Charter,

00:03:16.710 --> 00:03:20.250
are putting people in
concentration camps,

00:03:20.250 --> 00:03:23.610
or they're harvesting
organs from people deemed

00:03:23.610 --> 00:03:26.730
not necessary, or
they're forcing people

00:03:26.730 --> 00:03:32.130
to have abortions that don't fit
their idea of family planning,

00:03:32.130 --> 00:03:34.800
or they're bullying
their neighbors,

00:03:34.800 --> 00:03:39.360
or they illegally created a base
in the Spratly Islands, what is

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:41.290
the United Nations going to do?

00:03:41.290 --> 00:03:43.560
And the answer is they
can't do anything.

00:03:43.560 --> 00:03:48.180
In 2020, we saw an
international pandemic.

00:03:48.180 --> 00:03:51.930
And our United Nations
charter medical organization,

00:03:51.930 --> 00:03:54.480
the World Health
Organization, warned us

00:03:54.480 --> 00:03:56.310
from the very beginning--

00:03:56.310 --> 00:03:59.640
do not issue a travel
ban against China.

00:03:59.640 --> 00:04:02.220
And then, we learned that
the World Health Organization

00:04:02.220 --> 00:04:06.570
was essentially parroting or
mimicking what China wanted.

00:04:06.570 --> 00:04:07.980
And why did they do that?

00:04:07.980 --> 00:04:10.500
Because of Chinese money
and Chinese pressure.

00:04:10.500 --> 00:04:12.300
This is not an aberration.

00:04:12.300 --> 00:04:15.180
It's inherent in the
idea of global governance

00:04:15.180 --> 00:04:19.050
that there is always going to be
strong powers who have agendas

00:04:19.050 --> 00:04:22.050
that are not global
in scope, but they're

00:04:22.050 --> 00:04:23.220
national and sovereign.

00:04:23.220 --> 00:04:25.080
But if all the other
countries in the world

00:04:25.080 --> 00:04:28.930
surrender their sovereignty,
and one powerful nation doesn't,

00:04:28.930 --> 00:04:30.960
then they have to come
up with a mechanism

00:04:30.960 --> 00:04:32.760
of collective defense.

00:04:32.760 --> 00:04:36.950
And so far in the history
of man, that's never worked.

